        "title": "feat(ui): enable Swarm toggle in Labs",
        "body": "Closes #110325\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nSettings → Labs still hides the Swarm feature even though the supporting Swarm work has landed, leaving operators without a UI toggle for the available configuration.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis enables the existing Swarm Labs registry entry now that the prerequisite work from #110359 is landed and the `tools.swarm` schema is available. It uses the existing immediate-save Labs behavior and does not require a Gateway restart.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can enable or disable Swarm from Settings → Labs and open the Swarm documentation directly from the feature row.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/pages/labs/labs-page.test.ts` — 1 file passed, 4 tests passed.\n- The rendered Labs page test verifies two entries, enabled Code Mode and Swarm toggles, both documentation links, and no restart hint.\n- `pnpm format ui/src/pages/labs/labs-registry.ts ui/src/pages/labs/labs-page.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Autoreview: clean, no accepted or actionable findings.\n",
